WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.217
Receptionist (British female): Good morning, Westbridge University Residence. How can I help?

00:04.557 --> 00:08.350
Student (British male): Hello. I'm calling to complete my accommodation application.

00:08.650 --> 00:12.252
Receptionist (British female): Certainly. First, can I take your family name?

00:12.472 --> 00:15.969
Student (British male): It's Chen. C, H, E, N.

00:16.249 --> 00:18.424
Receptionist (British female): Thank you. And when will you arrive?

00:18.634 --> 00:23.955
Student (British male): On the fourteenth of October. I originally wrote the twelfth, but my flight changed.

00:24.245 --> 00:28.102
Receptionist (British female): Right, the fourteenth of October. Do you want a shared room?

00:28.312 --> 00:32.730
Student (British male): No, a single room, please. I need somewhere quiet to study.

00:33.020 --> 00:34.684
Receptionist (British female): Any dietary requirement?

00:34.894 --> 00:39.714
Student (British male): Yes, vegetarian. I eat dairy products, but no meat or fish.

00:40.074 --> 00:56.753
Receptionist (British female): Now, several facilities are included in the weekly fee. Every room has Wi-Fi, and residents can use the bicycle storage without charge. The laundry is available, but each wash costs three pounds. Breakfast is optional, and I'm afraid there is no gym in this building.

00:57.143 --> 00:59.790
Student (British male): That's fine. What documents do you need?

01:00.000 --> 01:10.612
Receptionist (British female): Please send a copy of your passport by email. You can show the original at reception when you arrive. The deposit must be paid by bank transfer. We cannot accept cash for that.

01:10.942 --> 01:14.151
Student (British male): I understand. What time can I collect my key?

01:14.361 --> 01:21.224
Receptionist (British female): Check-in begins at three p.m. You said your flight lands at two, so arriving around half past four should be comfortable.

01:21.544 --> 01:30.324
Student (British male): Great. I chose Westbridge because it is close to the science building. The city centre residence was newer, but it was much farther from my classes.

01:30.604 --> 01:34.029
Receptionist (British female): That makes sense. I'll email your confirmation today.
